ompeting in her sixth Olympic Games, first appearing in 1976 when trap shooting was a mixed event. She competed in Beijing but placed 11th in qualifying and did not make the final. Two other favorites, China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117256"} "Liu Yingzi"] " and San Marino’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117258"} "Daniela Del Din"] ", failed to make the final round, placing 12th and 15th, respectively. The qualifying leader was " [:a {:href "/athletes/117251"} "Zuzana Štefečeková"] " (SVK), who was also the world record holder. She was tied at 70 targets with Finland’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117253"} "Satu Mäkelä-Nummela"] ". In the final Mäkelä-Nummela hit 21 of 25 targets to win the gold medal in a big upset, with Štefečeková dropping back to the silver."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Preliminary Round"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {} "Final Shoot-Off 3-6"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1245"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117253"} "Satu Mäkelä-Nummela"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FIN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FIN.png"}] "FIN"]] [:td {} "70 (2)"] [:td {} "91 (1)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1685"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/117251"} "Zuzana Štefečeková"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SVK"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SVK.png"}] "SVK"]] [:td {} "70 (1)"] [:td {} "89 (2)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "1774"] [